{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OSS conformity audit (2026-08-10): the plan matches current practice in actively maintained projects. Instructor (13.7k stars) pins/bounds a narrow shard with explicit survivor/timeout budgets; DataDog maps changed tests to source and compares fresh base/head runs; PostHog gates a targeted PR shard; Trailmark cancels superseded PR runs and always reports results; GeoParquet schedules broad mutation, fails on tool/zero-mutant errors, retries setup only, and publishes artifacts.\n\nRebar intentionally tightens those patterns: no cached mutation verdicts, exact regression checks only for AST-identical units, fingerprints for accepted equivalent survivors, zero allowed timeouts, and diagnostic reruns that cannot turn red green. The targeted Gerrit gate plus weekly/manual sweep, separate no-tests ceilings, pinned runtime, bounded concurrency, and fail-closed vote wiring need no plan change."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786422643852980001,"uuid":"d2efbe5c-6505-4996-a089-fdc4123397e5"}